[{:db/id "q-71269/selection/b55fab1eb102a5d57c0a5a2e0c55108292008db52428694c418a63484d580176" :answer/id #uuid "eb89f0ce-7a3f-5319-a7ee-579a4fbb60eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71269/selection/43ffda529e765eee7ba335a7be277b97279a2e5469f5f58597ed2200aa4220d6" :answer/id #uuid "34a73aaa-8712-5c38-ba6a-d74ec3011a05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71269/selection/3481fa0020fc62af6aa3a1d7270d1344f631c0d44c91c5f89a79f28f2ceaa8c9" :answer/id #uuid "8f532964-059a-56c1-8751-a27bf1f4829e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,1,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71269/selection/f83299d27589bfcc3cc87f67c92e8a070ba238e28e91e441fce88840bee0cbd0" :answer/id #uuid "708b3e8a-7f69-5439-a602-c231abac9e14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71269/selection/4314709114467be4653e74c62e55f86d6dc824f8f7183f6288c43557f8e6e46a" :answer/id #uuid "87d707d9-d5f1-53ed-a5e1-0f9e11a83245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-1,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71269/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b744509a-aaf3-5773-a166-8fa33cb468e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71269/selection/43ffda529e765eee7ba335a7be277b97279a2e5469f5f58597ed2200aa4220d6" :answer-field/choices ["q-71269/selection/b55fab1eb102a5d57c0a5a2e0c55108292008db52428694c418a63484d580176" "q-71269/selection/43ffda529e765eee7ba335a7be277b97279a2e5469f5f58597ed2200aa4220d6" "q-71269/selection/3481fa0020fc62af6aa3a1d7270d1344f631c0d44c91c5f89a79f28f2ceaa8c9" "q-71269/selection/f83299d27589bfcc3cc87f67c92e8a070ba238e28e91e441fce88840bee0cbd0" "q-71269/selection/4314709114467be4653e74c62e55f86d6dc824f8f7183f6288c43557f8e6e46a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71269" :question/id #uuid "cd7b78c1-6586-5772-840d-06dfdf6ee176" :question/math-academy-id "q-71269" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $x=1$ and $y=-z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $x=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y=-z$ (or $y+z=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71269/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71269"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129169/selection/30b1874ca7d11bf43663a12481e859a5e56a808c3c924480ee784c951427eb40" :answer/id #uuid "233189a9-7cc7-5e9b-803f-c63e072b07b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,-6,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129169/selection/1833b12ae2f16643d8d2eb366277f3193bf59102036937e9470512d5eefa31cc" :answer/id #uuid "c6c42555-612f-5d59-97c5-5290598a877c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,-4,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129169/selection/05644ba154c607f4f9548053587aefcf06cb43a1b01886121093c98058359810" :answer/id #uuid "787a7445-1cb7-5ac5-950f-51a380eb447f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4,6,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129169/selection/9ee0ebefefbda51982b45b2d00994b279474efe85614492477db8e8c8fe43b29" :answer/id #uuid "d7e54162-e89b-5dbb-ae32-c766417ba3b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-6,4,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129169/selection/1d48d97901374ebf6585f706313235024c665cbefdaaaa413632c8df5a09a28d" :answer/id #uuid "44ddfb1d-f321-51e2-bdef-7bb63f8adccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,6,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129169/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69826181-e839-534d-8f04-811418b3d660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129169/selection/1d48d97901374ebf6585f706313235024c665cbefdaaaa413632c8df5a09a28d" :answer-field/choices ["q-129169/selection/30b1874ca7d11bf43663a12481e859a5e56a808c3c924480ee784c951427eb40" "q-129169/selection/1833b12ae2f16643d8d2eb366277f3193bf59102036937e9470512d5eefa31cc" "q-129169/selection/05644ba154c607f4f9548053587aefcf06cb43a1b01886121093c98058359810" "q-129169/selection/9ee0ebefefbda51982b45b2d00994b279474efe85614492477db8e8c8fe43b29" "q-129169/selection/1d48d97901374ebf6585f706313235024c665cbefdaaaa413632c8df5a09a28d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129169" :question/id #uuid "d0aedac8-4550-5f55-b4ac-09ba9ac8ed13" :question/math-academy-id "q-129169" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+3z-11=0 \\\\ 2x-2y-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x+3z-11=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-2y-5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,3⟩\\times ⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+6j-4k \\\\  & =⟨6,6,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129169/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129169"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129229/selection/32aba5bc18119f41b09e29413c90e0415607b3295636c892fc0b11a3273ef4f2" :answer/id #uuid "792797aa-dac9-5b13-8d48-232f5a08494b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=4,\\,b=⟨-1,-7,5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129229/selection/bcecef349a578c755001d43f546c39bee5442126a54e5fcc0972418097020163" :answer/id #uuid "ffc03c30-6c94-5d79-9ea3-0d3bab7e87e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-8,\\,b=⟨-7,5,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129229/selection/bd32d9593823a68fc6e20de13640b205ad5ca218b0fd75d97e09a53c449f1065" :answer/id #uuid "aad9b1ce-b023-529c-9ca6-2465308721f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=8,\\,b=⟨-7,-1,-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129229/selection/fdd3a1591abedfa1a1987849669d33aa5e649c7705f052c8e249a12ec660e5a9" :answer/id #uuid "c9d9707f-bbe3-5514-b6c7-4435b3b448b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=7,\\,b=⟨-8,-5,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129229/selection/da1d2e3cb2e901baff22a5f1493a9bc9c66643e7fc1c5faf24eb71740f1a5731" :answer/id #uuid "1eb79c25-6570-5656-8f4b-0aa89eb79556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-4,\\,b=⟨-5,-1,7⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129229/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "891db865-96ab-540e-b237-c18f5e352742" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129229/selection/bd32d9593823a68fc6e20de13640b205ad5ca218b0fd75d97e09a53c449f1065" :answer-field/choices ["q-129229/selection/32aba5bc18119f41b09e29413c90e0415607b3295636c892fc0b11a3273ef4f2" "q-129229/selection/bcecef349a578c755001d43f546c39bee5442126a54e5fcc0972418097020163" "q-129229/selection/bd32d9593823a68fc6e20de13640b205ad5ca218b0fd75d97e09a53c449f1065" "q-129229/selection/fdd3a1591abedfa1a1987849669d33aa5e649c7705f052c8e249a12ec660e5a9" "q-129229/selection/da1d2e3cb2e901baff22a5f1493a9bc9c66643e7fc1c5faf24eb71740f1a5731"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129229" :question/id #uuid "5d143e7a-cebc-5440-b9bb-3b483458d2cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-129229" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $x+3y-2z-8=0$ and $2x+y-3z-16=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation gives \n\n$$\nx+0-2z-8=0\\,⟹\\,x=2z+8,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ and $x=2z+8$ into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2z+8)+0-3z-16 & =0 \\\\ 4z+16-3z-16 & =0 \\\\ z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=2(0)+8=8$ and $a=⟨8,0,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+3y-2z-8=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,3,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+y-3z-16=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,3,-2⟩\\times ⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-7i-j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-7,-1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨8,0,0⟩+t⟨-7,-1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=8+0=8,$ and $b=⟨-7,-1,-5⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129229/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129229"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71446/selection/2cd46b60a7098fe2a5b2da1081baaa0ba28695d4041caa3c373b640ca9643100" :answer/id #uuid "fd8ed127-be85-544a-bc03-1806ffa03548" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-2,\\,b=⟨1,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71446/selection/33458ea9d62d6a16f92986a447bb501086b5eeaaa54a8ab6400af3f4de52a487" :answer/id #uuid "ada6b8f6-5526-5e24-ad84-0b05b1181052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-3,\\,b=⟨1,-2,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71446/selection/767b552d20fdb28d2c7c8284a5c3709da627c2a787a8551f4f67fa43a691fb44" :answer/id #uuid "e881c0c4-9a27-5d88-9335-7ba7bebb29d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨2,-2,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71446/selection/510810cac833bed9b0315e38e3a5d283e8f93fbf38e29319e1fe698e476e9d6a" :answer/id #uuid "bce644e9-3d29-5fa1-af4d-33771a072e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨-1,-2,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71446/selection/f0ddd7697eafdf71cb801606acfac7f23954419254a4866939d1c04b4a615785" :answer/id #uuid "2e11eee1-0155-5d84-96b6-03d1ea939615" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨1,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71446/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dddf3ab9-17c6-51d5-a9ad-06d3404c0068" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71446/selection/2cd46b60a7098fe2a5b2da1081baaa0ba28695d4041caa3c373b640ca9643100" :answer-field/choices ["q-71446/selection/2cd46b60a7098fe2a5b2da1081baaa0ba28695d4041caa3c373b640ca9643100" "q-71446/selection/33458ea9d62d6a16f92986a447bb501086b5eeaaa54a8ab6400af3f4de52a487" "q-71446/selection/767b552d20fdb28d2c7c8284a5c3709da627c2a787a8551f4f67fa43a691fb44" "q-71446/selection/510810cac833bed9b0315e38e3a5d283e8f93fbf38e29319e1fe698e476e9d6a" "q-71446/selection/f0ddd7697eafdf71cb801606acfac7f23954419254a4866939d1c04b4a615785"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71446" :question/id #uuid "61cf4d39-9683-533e-9394-f4988b6cbe81" :question/math-academy-id "q-71446" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $x+2y+3z=0$ and $3x+2y+z+8=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives    \n\n$$\nx+2(0)+3z=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3z,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ and $x=-3z$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z+8 & =0 \\\\ 3(-3z)+2(0)+z+8 & =0 \\\\ -8z & =-8 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-3z=-3$ and $a=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+2y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,2,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x+2y+z+8=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,2,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,2,3⟩\\times ⟨3,2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-4i+8j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n\n$$\nb=-\\frac{1}{4}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨1,-2,1⟩.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-3+1=-2,$ and $b=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71446/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71446"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129238/selection/1b95a5221b994926782c12dbbe6f11055500cc4c690dac439af3f463d20e9edf" :answer/id #uuid "2255437b-2a7c-5d4b-ad0d-c5342e87f421" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=3,\\,b=⟨-1,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129238/selection/316743ac95d05f87d2a5b2c1d2c33e1dfaa1a45dd0cfc14d06896a985a1667fa" :answer/id #uuid "6a9ec6e5-63a1-5ba1-aca6-2d683cb7adfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=6,\\,b=⟨-2,1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129238/selection/b9aff87cf5b36168cdade2c0601113aa6fd6d2208f31708313f838f65adf5954" :answer/id #uuid "1997b8a8-bf75-5ad1-9f36-d3435660bf7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-3,\\,b=⟨-1,1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129238/selection/61ae180caa56ae0caeed1ceff23c8afb601690a408b479243b09b664d6b1aa1d" :answer/id #uuid "b2667c7c-92a3-53f3-b37b-df98b05ec599" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=5,\\,b=⟨1,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129238/selection/7b7f013d7cd5341944af4a1cb9885e0fc08065aa94f8277d6c1ac7a6dfdbbc59" :answer/id #uuid "df20b430-25c3-5035-a27e-d4983f0fe92a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-6,\\,b=⟨-2,1,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129238/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1d2c490-607d-5fd2-bf7b-1eb2ec0dceb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129238/selection/1b95a5221b994926782c12dbbe6f11055500cc4c690dac439af3f463d20e9edf" :answer-field/choices ["q-129238/selection/1b95a5221b994926782c12dbbe6f11055500cc4c690dac439af3f463d20e9edf" "q-129238/selection/316743ac95d05f87d2a5b2c1d2c33e1dfaa1a45dd0cfc14d06896a985a1667fa" "q-129238/selection/b9aff87cf5b36168cdade2c0601113aa6fd6d2208f31708313f838f65adf5954" "q-129238/selection/61ae180caa56ae0caeed1ceff23c8afb601690a408b479243b09b664d6b1aa1d" "q-129238/selection/7b7f013d7cd5341944af4a1cb9885e0fc08065aa94f8277d6c1ac7a6dfdbbc59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129238" :question/id #uuid "d6407551-67a9-560e-b723-72e719f9cb5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-129238" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $x+y-z-3=0$ and $x+2y-3z+18=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives  \n\n$$\nx+y-0-3=0\\,⟹\\,x=3-y,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ and $x=3-y$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-y)+2y-3(0)+18 & =0 \\\\ 3+y+18 & =0 \\\\ y & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=3-y=3+21=24$ and $a=⟨24,-21,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+y-z-3=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,1,-1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x+2y-3z+18=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,1,-1⟩\\times ⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨24,-21,0⟩+t⟨-1,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=24-21=3,$ and $b=⟨-1,2,1⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129238/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129238"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-71112"] :question/problem "Given the two planes $-x-2y+z=0$ and $2x+4y-2z+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n- The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $-x-2y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+4y-2z+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${n}_{2}=-2{n}_{1}.$ So, the normal vectors are parallel.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFor the two planes to coincide, the equation of one plane should be a scalar multiple of the other. However, if we try to manipulate the equation of the second plane to resemble the equation of the first plane, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-2z+1=0 \\\\ x+2y-z+\\frac{1}{2}=0 \\\\ -x-2y+z-\\frac{1}{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nClearly, this equation is not the same as the equation of the first plane. So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-129261/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "bac37965-8c39-5fe8-8477-dca2f06947a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129261/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d0910555-34fd-5736-bb97-1bfe04b7cec3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129261/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f3baef66-cb25-55f8-9dcb-524cc89acc3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129261/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "434a6c0a-9995-57aa-ae40-2f5688e38d1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129261/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4967c162-3d17-5ddc-89c4-29461e0fb076" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129261/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ddbfadd-a8b1-5f1f-ad22-809f6ba2beaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129261/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-129261/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-129261/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-129261/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-129261/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-129261/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129261" :question/id #uuid "22e39499-5747-5698-af95-b4fc0c4d8191" :question/math-academy-id "q-129261" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-y+2z=0$ and $5x+y-13=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨-3,12,6⟩.$\n- The planes intersect on a line.\n- The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x+y-13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-1,2⟩\\times ⟨5,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i+10j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,10,6⟩\\ne ⟨-3,12,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129261/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129261"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71463/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "308325ff-1cef-5051-a5e8-80a4f61c1912" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71463/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "05509d3f-017b-515f-81bf-22b6415a40b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71463/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5c3bf136-3ab6-5529-91cb-fe72aa416075" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71463/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "9b4a1fc4-4222-51fe-b3da-0ee4c2222007" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71463/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5422e736-9203-5e36-af7d-46408e9f0d69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71463/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db363893-de21-563c-b1a8-bb84a9a85da9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71463/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-71463/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-71463/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-71463/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-71463/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-71463/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71463" :question/id #uuid "c0212fc2-f78c-514d-ac95-d9fd26dc0ceb" :question/math-academy-id "q-71463" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x+3y+2z=0$ and $x-y-z=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,6,-5⟩.$\n- The planes are parallel.\n- The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y-z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,3,2⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+5j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-6⟩\\ne ⟨1,6,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71463/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71463"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
